# Repo-root build context (issue #3938).
#
# This context is used by packages/api/Dockerfile (docker-compose.yml,
# ci:build-deploy-images, api:publish all build it with `-f packages/api/Dockerfile .`)
# and by the CI images under .gitlab/ci-images/ (api.Dockerfile, integration.Dockerfile,
# scheduler.Dockerfile, wasm.Dockerfile, keycloak.Dockerfile). None of those COPY
# .git, a virtualenv, node_modules, or local cache/env artifacts — they COPY only
# specific package subpaths (packages/scheduler/src, packages/api, pyproject.toml /
# README.md / CHANGELOG.md files, Cargo.toml/Cargo.lock, NOTICES/licenses/LICENSE/
# NOTICE, .gitlab/keycloak/trueppm-realm.json) — so excluding everything below is
# safe for all of them. None of the three published packages (scheduler, api, mcp)
# use hatch-vcs/setuptools-scm — versions are static in pyproject.toml — so .git is
# not needed by any build that uses this context.
#
# packages/web has its own .dockerignore scoped to its own (narrower) build context.

# Version control
.git
**/.git

# Python
.venv
**/.venv
venv
**/venv
__pycache__
**/__pycache__
*.py[cod]
**/*.py[cod]
*.egg-info
**/*.egg-info
.mypy_cache
**/.mypy_cache
.pytest_cache
**/.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
**/.ruff_cache
.hypothesis
**/.hypothesis
htmlcov
**/htmlcov

# Node (no trailing slash so a `scripts/wt`-created symlink is excluded too,
# not just a real directory — see the matching note in the repo's own .gitignore)
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Env files (may hold local secrets; never needed inside an image build)
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*

# Build output / caches not needed by any image build in this context
dist
**/dist
coverage
**/coverage
coverage.xml
**/coverage.xml
.astro
**/.astro
*.log
**/*.log
.scannerwork
**/.scannerwork

# Editor / OS cruft
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
.idea
**/.idea
.vscode
**/.vscode
